id: pm-f6zjpq
title: "Agent skills routed to a workflow loop but named no capability family and no read-cost, so four of twelve command families and the entire output-budget surface were unreachable through progressive disclosure"
description: "The four canonical skill bundles taught the claim-implement-close loop and routed to two references each. They named no capability map, so graph, assurance, merge, and the read-output budget family had no entry point at any tier; and they annotated no retrieval cost, so an agent could not tell that a routed document was 275 tokens or 45,000."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:agent-ux","area:docs",context-management,progressive-disclosure,skills
created_at: "2026-08-16T10:27:59.110Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T10:52:27.843Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-16T10:52:27.244Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-16T10:52:27.244Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "Every SKILL.md declares an explicit load order with measured per-tier costs; Every command family reachable from the CLI has an entry command and a guide topic named in at least one skill; pm guide covers the previously unrouted families so runtime routing does not depend on prose; Each skill's references are individually loadable, cost-annotated, and route into large documents by section rather than whole; A reference file that no SKILL.md links to fails the docs/skills gate; The author-detection and never-pass-author rule appears in every bundle"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Progressive disclosure is now explicit and measured: every tier declares its cost, every capability family has an entry point and a runtime guide topic, and an unreachable reference fails CI."
expected_result: "An agent can reach any pm capability through a bounded, cost-known expansion path."
actual_result: "Four capability families had no route, and no route declared its cost."
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-suhxny,discovered_from,"2026-08-16T10:27:59.110Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
  pm-1kxs,implements,"2026-08-16T10:37:54.910Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T10:29:20.025Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence: pm guide now returns 12 topics (was 8). docs/skills gate passes; negative control confirmed - adding an unlinked references/ORPHAN.md fails the gate with the exact path, removing it restores the pass. Claude plugin smoke passed. Measured routing costs recorded in each skill: SKILL.md ~650 tok, pm next ~2.5k, pm contracts --summary ~2.6k, pm guide <topic> --depth brief ~640 tok, docs/COMMANDS.md ~29k, docs/SDK.md ~45k."
  "2026-08-16T10:52:26.636Z","harness:claude-code","Coverage before and after, measured against docs/generated/AGENT_COMMAND_SURFACE.md (75 commands: 13 core, 22 standard, 36 full plus 4 internal).\n\nBefore, no skill named an entry point for four capability families: relationships (graph, deps), declared invariants (assurance, validate as a gate rather than a check), branch and fleet (merge, claim/release as concurrency primitives), and the entire read-output budget surface (--output-budget, --output-limit, --output-include, --output-cursor, --output-session, --output-format, --token-accounting). The last is the surface whose sole purpose is keeping an agent's context small, and it appeared in zero of twelve skill bundles.\n\nAlso absent from every bundle: the never-pass---author rule, despite it being an AGENTS.md non-negotiable and a user mandate.\n\nAfter: pm guide returns 12 topics (was 8). The four new topics - tokens, graph, assurance, merge - each carry commands, two workflow templates, and doc references verified to exist. Each of the four canonical SKILL.md files declares a load order with measured per-tier costs and a capability map naming an entry command and a guide topic per family. Eight harness plugin skills carry the same token-discipline and guide-routing block.\n\nMeasured routing costs now stated in the skills rather than implied: SKILL.md ~650 tok, pm guide <topic> --depth brief ~640 tok, pm list-open --limit 20 ~909 tok, pm context --limit 10 ~2,063 tok, pm next ~2,525 tok, pm contracts --summary ~2,637 tok, pm help ~3,136 tok, pm contracts --command list --flags-only ~3,372 tok, pm guide commands --depth standard ~7,981 tok, docs/COMMANDS.md ~28,980 tok, docs/SDK.md ~45,117 tok. Both large documents are now routed into by heading rather than linked whole; SURFACE_MAP.md and AUTHORING.md carry the heading indexes.\n\nGate: validateSkillReferenceReachability fails when a references/*.md is not linked from its own SKILL.md. Negative control proven - an unlinked ORPHAN.md fails naming the exact path, removing it restores the pass. The gate already runs in CI via docs.yml and release.yml.\n\nVerification: docs/skills gate passed, Claude plugin smoke passed, full test suite passed, pnpm quality:static passed."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  scripts/release/docs-skills-gate.mjs,project,Fails when a reference file is unreachable from its SKILL.md
  src/sdk/guide-topics.ts,project,"Adds the tokens,graph,assurance,and merge guide topics"
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  node scripts/release/docs-skills-gate.mjs,project,300
